390	517	Early life
Hadja Lahbib was born on 21 June 1970 in Boussu, near the city of Mons, to a Francophone family of Algerian Kabyles.
518	604	Her parents are practicing Muslims, but she says she is more attracted to Buddhism.



604	786	Career as a journalist
Lahbib graduated in journalism from the Free University of Brussels and worked for a long time for the Belgian Radio-Television of the French Community (RTBF).
787	923	In particular, she was a special correspondent in Afghanistan and the Middle East, and presented the television news for two decades.



923	1089	Journey to Crimea as a journalist

Before starting her political career, Hadja Lahbib visited the politically disputed Crimea between Russia and Ukraine in July 2021.
